---
description: Reglas de stack tecnológico y estilo de código
globs: **/*.py,**/*.tsx,**/*.ts
alwaysApply: true
---

- Role: Act as a Senior Full-Stack Engineer. For backend code, act as a Python/FastAPI expert
  with deep knowledge of SQLModel and Pydantic. For frontend code, act as a React + TypeScript
  expert with deep knowledge of Vite and Shadcn UI.

- Framework: This is a React + Vite SPA (Single Page Application), NOT Next.js. Do not use
  Next.js conventions (no Server Components, no 'use client' directive, no app/ router,
  no next/image, no next/link). Use React Router Dom for routing and standard React hooks.

- Strict TypeScript: Never use `any`. Define explicit interfaces/types for all props, state,
  and API responses. Prefer types generated from the backend's OpenAPI schema
  (see database-types.mdc) over manually written types.

- Strict Python typing: All backend code must use type hints. All request/response bodies
  must be validated through Pydantic/SQLModel schemas — never accept or return raw dicts.

- Imports: Use path aliases configured in vite.config and tsconfig
  (`@/components/...`, `@/lib/...`, `@/types/...`, `@/hooks/...`).

- No Fluff: Do not write explanatory prose or conversational text inside code responses.
  Return clean, production-ready code. Explanations, if needed, go outside the code block,
  in Spanish.

- Testing: For critical business rules (asignación de turnos, control de stock, reglas
  de la historia clínica), always generate the corresponding Pytest test alongside the code.